---
/*
  Selection as positioning, with the second entry point for the creator who
  lost an account set at the same weight, same size, same spacing.
  04-konzept.md section 4.3, page "/who-we-work-with", and section 3.
  The internal exclusions (professional performers, media contracts) stay off
  this page on purpose. They belong in qualification, not in public copy.
  Sprache: einfaches Englisch, Ansage Manuel 07.09.2026 abends.
*/
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBlock from '../components/CtaBlock.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Who we work with | Wunder"
  description="What we look for, in public, and what we do when you have lost an account before."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>We say no more often than yes.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Here is what we look at. Check yourself against it, before you spend twenty minutes on a
        call.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Steady reach, not a follower count. Last month counts more than three years of collecting.</li>
        <li>A live OnlyFans link that is yours.</li>
        <li>Content in English.</li>
        <li>A face people can see. We do not run an AI persona.</li>
        <li>Reach you did not buy.</li>
        <li>You pay tax in the European Union.</li>
        <li>Time for the posting rhythm we agree on. This is the one we say no over most.</li>
      </ul>
      <CtaBlock />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>If you have lost an account before.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        You are not starting at zero. You are building back an account that worked once. This time
        you can see every step we take.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most people we work with have had at least one agency. Some of those agencies were bad.
        That is not a no here. We want to know the history of the account. We want to know how you
        lost it. We would rather hear both at the start than in month three.
      </p>
      <p>
        Maybe your last month was quiet because you stopped posting. Say so in the form. It
        changes the plan, not the answer.
      </p>
      <CtaBlock />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Who we do not take on.</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Anyone who pays tax outside the European Union. We cannot pay you the way we pay the rest.</li>
        <li>
          Anyone still tied to another agency or manager, until that deal ends. See <a
            href="/switching">switching</a
          >.
        </li>
        <li>Accounts with reach that was bought.</li>
        <li>Faceless accounts and AI personas.</li>
        <li>Anyone who wants us to run the account alone. There is no version of this without you.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
